ts=2026-09-07T13:26:41.671Z type=context scope=user content="important facts automatically\n* Memory manager (view, edit, delete)\n* Toggle memory on/off\n\n### Project Workspace\n\n* Open any folder\n* Read project files\n* Search project\n* Attach files\n* Drag-and-drop support\n* Multiple project workspaces\n\n### Coding Agent\n\n* Read files\n* Create files\n* Edit files\n* Rename files\n* Delete files\n* Run terminal commands\n* View command output\n* Apply code diffs with approval\n* Git status\n* Commit support\n* Explain code\n* Refactor code\n\n### Tools\n\n* PDF reader\n* Image viewer\n* OCR\n* JSON viewer\n* Markdown preview\n* File preview\n\n### Prompt Library\n\n* Save prompts\n* Categories\n* Favorites\n* Variables/templates\n* One-click execution\n\n### Model Router\n\n* Allow manual model selection\n* Optional automatic routing based on task type\n\n### UI\n\n* Dark/light mode\n* Resizable sidebar\n* Keyboard shortcuts\n* Tabs\n* Settings page\n* Notifications\n* Responsive layout\n\n### Local Storage\n\n* SQLite database\n* Automatic backups\n* Restore backups\n* Import/export settings\n\n## Requirements\n\n* Modular architecture\n* Clean code\n* No placeholder implementations\n* No mock data\n* No unfinished features\n* Every feature must be fully functional\n* Type-safe\n* Lint clean\n* Build clean\n* Production ready\n\n## Important\n\nDo not generate fake implementations.\n\nWhen a feature depends on an external API, implement the integration completely and expose a settings page where I can paste my own API keys later.\n\nContinue building until every feature above is implemented, tested, and integrated into a single working application. ## Workspace System\n\n* Workspace-first architecture.\n* Open any folder as a workspace.\n* Each workspace has independent:\n\n  * Chats\n  * Memory\n  * Settings\n  * Prompt history\n  * AI context\n* Also include a Global Chat that is not attached to any workspace.\n\n---\n\n## Usage Dashboard\n\nCreate a dedicated Usage page.\n\nFor every configured provider display:\n\n* Provider name\n* Selected model\n* Connection status\n* API key status (masked)\n* Total requests\n* Successful requests\n* Failed requests\n* Tokens sent\n* Tokens received\n* Total tokens\n* Estimated API cost (when possible)\n* Remaining credits/quota if the provider exposes it\n* Remaining request limits if available\n* Requests per minute\n* Requests per day\n* Last request time\n* Average response time\n* Streaming status\n* Current active model\n\nDisplay all values using clean progress bars and percentage indicators where supported.\n\nIf a provider does not expose usage or quota information, clearly label those values as \"Not provided by provider\" and estimate only what can be inferred locally.\n\n---\n\n## Quality of Life\n\n* Auto-save everything\n* Crash recovery\n* Restore previous session\n* Unlimited local chats\n* Unlimited workspaces\n* Unlimited prompt library\n* Unlimited memories (limited only by disk space)\n* Fast global search\n* Workspace search\n* Keyboard shortcuts\n* Drag-and-drop attachments\n* Conversation branching\n* Pin chats\n* Archive chats\n* Favorites\n* Import/export chats\n* Import/export settings\n* Automatic local backups\n* Portable mode\n* Permission prompts before file edits or terminal execution\n\n---\n\n## Extensibility\n\nDesign the application so adding a new OpenAI-compatible provider requires only:\n\n* Provider name\n* Base URL\n* API key\n* Model\n\nNo application code changes should be required.\n\n---\n\n## Performance\n\n* Handle thousands of chats smoothly.\n* Handle hundreds of workspaces.\n* Fast search.\n* Lazy loading.\n* Streaming UI.\n* Efficient local database.\n* Responsive interface.\n\n---\n\n## Production Standard\n\nThe final application should feel comparable in polish to modern desktop AI tools.\n\nEvery feature must be fully integrated.\n\nNo placeholders.\n\nNo unfinished pages.\n\nNo mock data.\n\nNo demo implementations.\n\nNo TODOs.\n\nNo fake functionality.\n\nEverything must be fully functional and tested before completion. use whatever required and get the job done ASAP" tags=auto
ts=2026-09-07T18:08:54.146Z type=context scope=user content="- Window size\n- Window position\n- Maximized state\n\nRestore them automatically.\n\n5. Auto Restore\nWhen reopening:\n- Restore last chat.\n- Restore last provider.\n- Restore last model.\n- Restore last opened project.\n\n6. Error Handling\nIf Electron cannot start:\n- Show a friendly dialog.\n- Never leave the user with a blank window.\n\n7. Documentation\nCreate a QUICK_START.md containing:\n\n- Installation\n- First launch\n- How to start the app\n- How to update\n- Troubleshooting\n\n8. Final Verification\n\nVerify:\n\n✓ npm run dev\n✓ npm run build\n✓ npm run start\n✓ launch-ai-workspace.bat\n✓ Desktop shortcut works\n✓ Window restores\n✓ Previous chat restores\n\nGenerate a short report and STOP.\n\nDo not implement anything else." tags=auto
